00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:12.509
Right.

00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:14.310
And I said, yeah.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.359
And the story there is that I had spent a
lot of time as a young, ambitious correspondent

00:01:18.359 --> 00:01:20.670
in war zones after 9/11.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.539
I was in Iraq and Afghanistan, et cetera,
et cetera.

00:01:23.539 --> 00:01:28.310
And I'd come home, gotten depressed, and I
didn't even know I was depressed and then

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.020
blindly self medicated with recreational drugs.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.369
And even though I wasn't high on the air and
I wasn't even doing drugs, that frequently

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:39.899
was enough to change my brain chemistry per
this doctor.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:43.489
And so that was a big wakeup call for me and
had a lot of positive impact.

00:01:43.489 --> 00:01:49.509
And so when this happens, when the actual
acute incident happened, you believe that

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:57.429
it was because of other it wasn't the stress
